Eric Harrison wrote:
>
> We were talking about "*Bane" weapons in #nethack and someone brought
> up the painful nature of insects (specifically soldier ants) and that
> there should be an "Insectbane".
>
> It gave me this silly idea which I thought I'd share with you:
>
> The Flyswatter, an artifact hammer that deals double damage against
> all insects.

One way to nerf the super artifacts is to increase the number of junk
artifacts.  I rather like the idea of having a nerf version of a super
artifact.  Grayswandir/Werebane, Mjollnir/Orgesmasher,
Stormbringer/Dragonbane(Orcrist), Magicbane/Sting.  Going through the
current list I think the axe category is the missing one, Cleaver has no
nerf artifact competitor.

It would be pretty funny for Flyswatter to be an axe.  And ThinkMole as
a double speed tunneler might be considered useful but end up having
folks tunnel more without actually improving their games.

> Now, truthfully, by the time you reach a coaligned altar and are able
> to start getting sacrifice gifts insects are rarely a problem anymore,
> but I still think it would be nice to ascend with an artifact weapon
> that shows how much you hate Team a. :D

That's typical Nethack poetry!


